"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunk_8x8_developer_docs=globalThis.webpackChunk_8x8_developer_docs||[]).push([[17685],{38062:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"id":"2026-10-13-whatsapp-service-message-charging","date":"2026-10-13","products":["Connect"],"product":"Connect","channel":"WhatsApp","changeType":"Changed","title":"WhatsApp pricing: service messages and in-window Utility templates now charged","excerpt":"The WhatsApp docs now reflect Meta\'s pricing change effective October 1, 2026. Two kinds of message that were free inside an open 24-hour Customer Service Window (CSW) are now charged per delivered message.","hasArticle":true,"bodyHtml":"<p>The WhatsApp docs now reflect Meta&#39;s pricing change effective <strong>October 1, 2026</strong>. Two kinds of message that were free inside an open 24-hour Customer Service Window (CSW) are now charged per delivered message.</p>\\n<h2>What&#39;s charged now</h2>\\n<table>\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th>Message sent inside the CSW</th>\\n<th>Before</th>\\n<th>From October 1, 2026</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody><tr>\\n<td><strong>Service message</strong> (non-template / freeform reply)</td>\\n<td>Free</td>\\n<td>Charged at the service message rate, after the monthly free tier</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td><strong>Utility template</strong></td>\\n<td>Free</td>\\n<td>Charged at the Utility rate for the recipient&#39;s market</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody></table>\\n<ul>\\n<li><strong>Service message rate</strong> is the same as the market&#39;s Utility and Authentication rate. Service messages don&#39;t qualify for volume tiers.</li>\\n<li><strong>Monthly free tier:</strong> each business phone number gets 1,000 free service messages per month, and 8x8 passes this on to you. Unused messages don&#39;t roll over. Charging starts at the 1,001st service message in the month.</li>\\n<li><strong>One charge per message:</strong> a non-template message with promotional content is still a service message. Meta doesn&#39;t add a Marketing charge.</li>\\n<li><strong>Free Entry Point window</strong> is not affected and still makes all messages free. It now opens only from a Click-to-WhatsApp ad (Android or iOS app) and can stay open for up to <strong>7 days</strong>, replacing the previous 72-hour description.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<h2>Reporting</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Delivery receipts now list the <code>pricingCategory</code> values: <code>marketing</code>, <code>utility</code>, <code>authentication</code>, <code>authentication_international</code>, and <code>service</code> (non-template messages). A new sample shows a delivered service message.</li>\\n<li><code>pricingCategory</code> doesn&#39;t tell you whether an individual message was free. Use the Message Usage API for <code>free</code> and <code>charged</code> counts by pricing category.</li>\\n<li>Messaging Apps reports now count free and chargeable traffic per message instead of per conversation.</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>The glossary adds <strong>Service Message</strong>, <strong>Free Entry Point Window</strong>, and <strong>Volume Tier</strong>. The Coexistence guide notes that freeform messages sent through the Cloud API are chargeable.</p>\\n<h2>Read more</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\"/connect/docs/whatsapp/concepts-fundamentals\\">Concepts &amp; Fundamentals</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"/connect/docs/delivery-receipts-for-outbound-chatapps\\">Delivery receipts for Outbound Messaging Apps</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"/connect/reference/get-message-usage\\">Get message usage</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n"}')}}]);